"""Remote service planning briefs; no office or client claims."""

city_rows = [
('Indore','indore','commerce and service comparison','retail brands and professional teams','Indore businesses often combine in-store relationships with digital discovery. A website can help a customer compare offerings before a visit or enquiry.','A visitor should see the actual product or service categories, availability context and a direct path to ask for details. Avoid making every category a separate thin page.','Organize meaningful categories, show real product or service detail and connect each one to the right enquiry route.','For a growing catalog, decide who updates prices and descriptions. The content model should remain manageable as the range changes.','Would a catalog or full store suit this project?','That depends on whether customers need to buy online or only understand the range and enquire. Payments, inventory and fulfilment add operational work.'),
('Bhopal','bhopal','clear institutional information','education and professional service teams','A site serving students, families or professional clients needs trustworthy information that is easy to check. Policy, timing and process details may change over time.','Someone arriving on an inner page should know which organization is speaking, what the next step is and where to find official updates.','Separate admissions or service information from announcements, then give each a clear owner and update rhythm.','Build accessible navigation and readable documents. Verify that forms ask only for necessary information and explain what happens after submission.','How can notices stay current?','An editing workflow and an assigned content owner help. A dated announcement archive can preserve context without crowding the main pages.'),
('Mumbai','mumbai','focused positioning in a crowded market','specialists and independent firms','A broad offer can disappear among many similar search results. A website for a Mumbai service firm should explain its specific fit and show evidence for the work it actually does.','A visitor comparing providers wants scope, examples, process and a practical way to start. Claims about being the best rarely answer these questions.','Write distinct pages around real offerings and demonstrate the outcome with selected case studies or verifiable credentials.','Keep the first screen concise, make mobile contact easy and use precise location and service-area language where it is accurate.','Can a remote developer build for a Mumbai business?','Yes. Discovery, design reviews and delivery can happen remotely. Local business facts and customer insight should come from your team.'),
('Bengaluru','bengaluru','product explanation and conversion','software teams and startups','A product site needs to communicate a complicated idea before the visitor gives up. Feature lists alone can hide the main job the product performs.','Different visitors may be evaluating fit, integration, pricing or implementation. The route between those questions should feel deliberate.','Lead with the use case, pair product detail with proof and make a demo or signup action relevant to the visitor stage.','Think through states such as empty data, errors and success messages alongside the marketing pages. Those details shape trust once a trial begins.','Can the marketing site and product UI share a design system?','Yes. Shared typography, color and component rules can create continuity while each surface serves a different task.'),
('Delhi','delhi','service credibility and navigation','consultants and multi-service businesses','A multi-service firm may need to speak to several audiences without turning the home page into a directory of vague promises.','Visitors who know the service they need should reach a useful dedicated page quickly; first-time visitors need a concise overview.','Group related services, explain each with scope and process, and connect claims to real team experience or work examples.','Make enquiries route to the right conversation. A simple service selection can reduce back-and-forth without making the form long.','Should each service have a separate landing page?','Only if it has distinct scope, examples and buyer questions. A repeated page with a swapped keyword is unlikely to help users.'),
('Pune','pune','recruitment and business clarity','growing companies and B2B teams','A growing company site often serves buyers and job applicants at the same time. Mixing both journeys into one generic page can frustrate each audience.','A buyer wants capabilities and evidence; a candidate wants role details, culture and an application route.','Create clear paths for services, selected work and careers, with the most important information visible on mobile.','Treat careers content as maintained content rather than a static badge. Archived roles and current opportunities should be clearly distinguished.','Can one site support clients and candidates?','Yes. Use clear navigation and distinct calls to action so each audience can find the information meant for them.'),
('Hyderabad','hyderabad','technical service explanation','technology providers and agencies','Technical buyers often arrive with specific questions about capabilities, integration and delivery. A polished slogan cannot replace enough detail to evaluate fit.','Explain supported workflows, boundaries and handoff. Where possible, show actual work instead of generic diagrams.','Structure services by the problem solved, link to relevant case studies and document the steps from brief to delivery.','Make technical claims precise, and keep product or platform references current as they change.','What belongs in a technical case study?','The goal, your role, constraints, approach and outcome are useful. Avoid metrics that cannot be verified.'),
('Chennai','chennai','accessible bilingual-ready content structure','manufacturers and service organizations','A service site may have complex offerings, specifications and regional audiences. Visitors need an organized route to the right product or contact.','If more than one language is needed, translation should be planned as content work, not treated as an automatic switch with unchecked output.','Create a product or service taxonomy with clear detail pages and a reliable enquiry context.','Plan language versions around actual content ownership, translated navigation and properly matched URLs when both are published.','Can the site support more than one language?','Yes, if accurate translated content and a maintenance owner are available. We can plan the URL and navigation structure before implementation.'),
('Kolkata','kolkata','editorial storytelling with clear action','creators and heritage businesses','A brand with a rich story can attract attention, but visitors still need to find products, services and practical buying details.','The story should help someone understand origin and value, then make the next action obvious rather than burying it in long prose.','Pair concise narrative sections with meaningful collections, descriptive images and straightforward contact or purchase options.','Optimize media so the experience remains usable on modest connections. Alt text should describe the image rather than repeat keywords.','How much story should appear on the home page?','Enough to establish the brand and guide the visitor onward. Deeper history can live on an about page for those who want it.'),
('Ahmedabad','ahmedabad','structured product discovery','manufacturers and distributors','Buyers comparing industrial or wholesale offerings need specifications and enquiry context, not a decorative grid alone.','A category page should explain the range, while an individual product page should answer dimensions, use and availability where known.','Build a maintainable catalog with clear categories and an enquiry that carries the selected item.','Agree on who updates product data and what needs review before publication. Accurate information can reduce repetitive sales calls.','Is ecommerce necessary for a B2B catalog?','Not always. A quote request can fit products with variable pricing, configuration or minimum orders.'),
('Jaipur','jaipur','visual commerce with useful detail','craft and hospitality brands','Strong imagery can draw interest, but it needs accurate descriptions, availability and a path to book or buy.','A visitor may browse on a phone, then revisit to compare options. Clear collections and useful details support both sessions.','Give each meaningful offering its own content, use real photography where available and keep booking or purchase actions consistent.','Image compression, dimensions and loading behavior matter especially on visually rich pages. Plan for speed while retaining the brand character.','How do we make a visual site load quickly?','Use appropriately sized images, modern formats where supported and selective motion. Measure the finished pages on real devices.'),
('Surat','surat','catalog and enquiry workflow','textile and trade businesses','A large range can become hard to navigate if every item looks identical and basic specifications are missing.','Buyers need filtering or clear categories, relevant product facts and a way to ask about quantities or variations.','Start with the actual purchasing questions and create category and item templates around those details.','Keep the enquiry tied to the selected item. A clear reference in the message helps the team respond accurately.','Can the catalog start small and expand?','Yes. A stable category structure and consistent fields make later additions easier to manage.'),
('Lucknow','lucknow','service trust and appointment flow','professional practices and local services','People seeking a professional service often need to know scope, qualifications and the first step before they share personal details.','The page should explain the process in plain language and make contact possible without requiring an oversized form.','Separate services where the questions truly differ, add real background and keep contact choices straightforward.','Avoid unsupported outcomes and keep sensitive claims reviewed. Accessibility and mobile readability matter throughout the decision.','What information should an initial enquiry request?','Only what is needed to route and answer the request. Explain the next step and use a suitable channel for sensitive details.'),
('Chandigarh','chandigarh','portfolio proof and lead quality','design studios and consultants','A portfolio can look striking yet fail to explain the role, scope or result behind a project.','Prospective clients need enough context to decide if the same kind of work is relevant to them.','Show a curated set of real projects with clear responsibilities, practical details and an enquiry that invites a useful brief.','Use motion to guide attention between sections, and ensure the content works with reduced motion settings.','How many case studies should launch?','A few detailed, accurate examples are often more useful than a large wall of unexplained images.'),
('Nagpur','nagpur','straightforward local service discovery','regional service providers','A regional business may receive visitors from several nearby areas, each with slightly different service expectations.','Visitors need to know what is actually covered, what is offered and when a response can be expected.','Create a clear coverage explanation and detailed core services; add area content only when it answers a distinct question.','Keep names, contact details and hours accurate across the website and any business profiles you manage.','Do I need a page for every area?','No. Start with a useful coverage page. Separate pages make sense when there is genuinely distinct information for each place.'),
('Patna','patna','course and enrollment clarity','educators and training providers','Course pages can accumulate lists of topics without helping a student judge level, schedule or fit.','A student may need prerequisites, format, fees or a question answered before enrolling.','Give each substantial course a clear outcome, curriculum summary and enrolment or enquiry path.','Keep batch dates and terms current. Outdated dates undermine trust even when the rest of the design looks polished.','Can the team update batches themselves?','Yes. We can choose an editing workflow suited to how often schedules change and who manages them.'),
('Bhubaneswar','bhubaneswar','booking details and local discovery','wellness and appointment businesses','Someone considering an appointment wants to understand the service, duration, location and how booking works.','A landing page should answer those questions before asking for contact details. Real imagery and service specifics are more useful than repeated location phrases.','Structure service pages around differences in treatment, time and preparation, then connect each to booking.','Keep availability and service claims accurate. If the business operates from one address, show it clearly without implying other branches.','Should every neighborhood have its own page?','Only when each page offers meaningful local information and the business truly serves it. One clear service-area page can be stronger.'),
('Kochi','kochi','experience planning and booking confidence','travel and experience brands','Experience pages need to balance mood with logistics. People should know what is included, timing and how to reserve.','A visitor comparing options may return to check details; those facts should remain easy to find on every device.','Organize experiences by genuine differences and pair each with schedule, inclusions and clear enquiry or booking.','Use authentic media carefully and keep image weight controlled. Make policy details legible before a customer commits.','Can I launch without online payment?','Yes. A reliable enquiry or reservation workflow can be the first step, with payments added when operations support them.'),
('Raipur','raipur','supplier information and qualified enquiries','industrial and regional suppliers','A supplier site should help a buyer identify fit before sending a broad request. Product detail and delivery context can save time on both sides.','A visitor needs categories, specifications where available and an enquiry route that captures the required quantity or use.','Build a clear range, useful product templates and contact prompts tied to the item or service.','Prioritize accurate claims and maintainable information. Search pages should match actual products and service reach.','Would a downloadable catalog be enough?','A PDF may help sharing, but searchable HTML pages are easier to navigate and update. Both can serve different purposes.'),
('Gwalior','gwalior','credible first website','independent professionals and small firms','A first website often acts as a reference after a personal introduction. It should confirm the offer and make the next conversation easy.','A visitor wants a concise explanation, real background and reliable contact details rather than a page full of vague awards.','Start with a focused home page and meaningful service detail; expand when there are real projects or questions to publish.','Choose an editing approach that fits the owner. A small site still deserves mobile checks, descriptive metadata and working contact links.','How much content is enough for launch?','Enough to explain the services, audience, process and contact. Add more pages when there is distinct, useful information.'),
('Kanpur','kanpur','practical service and product navigation','manufacturers and repair businesses','Buyers often arrive knowing a specific product or problem. The website should help them confirm fit quickly.','A useful page answers scope, specifications or service coverage and tells the buyer what information to send.','Arrange content by real categories and common requests, then connect them to a qualified enquiry.','Avoid duplicating almost identical product pages. Use shared category information and unique item details where they exist.','Should I add a quote form?','Yes, if the sales team can respond and the form collects the few facts needed to prepare a relevant reply.'),
('Guwahati','guwahati','regional coverage and mobile usability','regional services and growing brands','A regional offer may extend beyond one city. The site should communicate its actual coverage without pretending to have a branch in every place.','Visitors should understand what is available, how delivery or appointments work and whom to contact.','Make coverage and service distinctions explicit, with original detail where the offering changes by area.','Design for variable connection quality and keep the main information in readable HTML. Remote collaboration can support build and updates.','Can one site cover a wider region?','Yes. A clear coverage page and well-organized services can explain the reach without dozens of repetitive city pages.'),
('Vadodara','vadodara','B2B capability communication','engineering and professional firms','A capabilities page should show what the team can actually deliver, not merely list broad industries.','Technical visitors may need process, certifications or specification ranges before they make contact.','Create service or capability pages with concrete scope and link each to verifiable work or documentation.','Use a concise enquiry that captures the requirement and routes it to the right person; keep technical details current.','How do we show work under confidentiality?','Use approved, anonymized descriptions of the problem and role, or focus on process and capabilities without disclosing restricted details.'),
('Visakhapatnam','visakhapatnam','service and logistics transparency','logistics and coastal businesses','A service site can reduce uncertainty by explaining coverage, process and the information required for a quote.','A buyer wants realistic scope and response expectations before sending business details.','Use focused service pages with process steps and a form or WhatsApp path that carries the relevant route or requirement.','Keep operational claims reviewed as coverage changes. A map or visual should clarify, not replace readable service information.','Can the website give instant quotes?','Only if pricing rules and data are reliable. A guided enquiry may be more appropriate when requirements vary.'),
]
cities=[dict(zip(('name','slug','focus','audience','context','visitor','plan','detail','question','answer'),r)) for r in city_rows]
